ecting a flip.", "watch": "A polling correction toward the narrower Democratic-sponsored summer surveys, or Barrett gaining traction on data centers and health care, could pull the race back to a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Barrett (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Michigan's 7th District pairs Republican incumbent Tom Barrett against Democrat William Lawrence in an even partisan split seat. The national midterm environment favors Democrats, and the race has drawn exceptional attention: it is the nation's most expensive House contest for advertising, with outside groups spending heavily against Barrett. Lawrence has leaned on union backing and proposals like a data-center moratorium and phased Medicare expansion, while Barrett campaigns on data-center transparency, health care changes and limits on war powers.\n\nRecent independent polling shows Lawrence ahead by about eight points, though Democratic-sponsored surveys earlier in the year showed a much narrower race. Raters are split between tossup and Democratic lean, with several expecting a flip, and prediction markets price Lawrence's chances around 70-78 percent. Barrett's incumbency and fundraising keep him competitive, but the weight of the evidence points to a modest Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7073, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7167, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7145, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10